diagnostics/list-min-max.em:1:21: `min_max` needs a List of ordered values, but this is [Bool]
  print([true, false].min_max())
                      ^^^^^^^
Ints, Floats, Strings, and types that adopt `Ordered` have an order. Use another operation for these elements.
diagnostics/list-min-max.em:3:21: `min_max` cannot choose from [Int?], whose elements may be absent
  print(maybe_numbers.min_max())
                      ^^^^^^^
Use `filter_map` to remove absent values first, so `nothing` can remain the empty-List result.
diagnostics/list-min-max.em:4:11: `min_max` takes 0 arguments, but this call passes 1
  print([1].min_max(1))
            ^^^^^^^
Match the number of arguments to what the method needs.
